<!--


-NEW MAJOR FEATURE: PLANT MUTATION
	-You can now directly infuence the outcome of plants by infusing them with saps you discover.
	-These plants will usually begin as standard, basic plants that have a tag which states their MUTATION POTENTIAL.
	-MUTATION POTENTIAL is shorthand for what saps it can be infused with. Plants can have a mutation potenial of None, Low, Medium, High, and Extreme.
	-'Higher' mutation potential = being able to accept stronger, rarer saps, which means the more outcomes you can get.
	-What you infuse into a mutatable plant will impact what kind of plants, structures, and even items something can produce.
	-You will need to partially master a genome before you can mutate it's plants. 'Mastering' a genome is done by researching specifically-named techs.
	-For example, to start infusing basic saps, you will need to research 'basic mutation applications'. For stronger, rarer saps, you research 'advanced mutation applications'
	-Depending on the genome's potential, these techs can have relatively high research requirements.
	-Whenever you discover a new sap, you will also need to 'study' it of them before it can be used for any infusions. This only needs to be done once per sap, however.
	-There is no cheat sheet on what infusions do what, but all outcomes have a positive output. Experiment!
	-Not everything will be infusable right off the bat. Due to the scope of the mod, more and more things will be infusable as time passes.

  -All organic weapons also have mutation potential. However, at this time the plants don't get infused and instead the weapons are infused at a terravat.
    -This will change once the code can be reviewed for flaws.
  -This follows the same pattern of potential (from None to Extreme), but the potential decreases by 2 as the weapon grows.
    -For example, if a genome has a potential of High, the potential of the immature weapon will be Low, and the mature weapon will be None.
    -Prima is exempt from this, which only has it's potential decrease by 1 as the weapon grows.

